Parity coverage:
  - Data sources bound via shared P1/S8 state holders (no HTTP in the view):
    VehicleSystemsStore.climateHistory (useClimateHistory), useVehicles vehicle
    id, useUnits (SI->display °C at the render boundary only), useDateFormat
    (injected time formatter), useTranslation (LocalizedStringKey), Resource ->
    LoadableState cache-then-network projection.
  - States reproduced (every one renders — never a blank box): loading
    (skeleton chrome), content, empty ("No climate history"), error
    (QueryError + retry), stale (freshness chip), offline (cached rows + offline
    chip), plus compact (size.cols<=1) and regular/wide.
  - i18n keys: widget.climateHistory.{title,displayName,description,cabin,
    outside,noData,error}, widget.action.refresh, widget.freshness.error
    (+ reused widget.freshness.{stale,offline}). No English string literals in
    native code.
  - Registry: id "climate-history", category "climate", default 2x4, min 2x4,
    max 4x40 (clamp enforced + unit-tested).
  - Telemetry: emits the shared typed taxonomy TelemetryEvent.ScreenView
    (stable name "screen_view") carrying surface slug "ClimateHistoryWidget"
    via the consent-gated Telemetry sink (ADR-016). The P1/S11 taxonomy has no
    free-form "view.opened" variant; ScreenView(screen:) is its contract-faithful
    encoding of a surface open.
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the refresh control, freshness chip, stat
    pills and the chart (latest cabin/outside summary); Dynamic Type via Font.TS;
    reduce-motion respected by the reused shared components.

